Page 14-after line 12 Insert:
"9-25-104. Jails; changing areas exclusively for members of a single sex.
(a) In each jail:
(i) Every shower room, sleeping quarters and restroom shall be
designated for use exclusively by males or exclusively by females;
(ii) Every shower room, sleeping quarters and restroom designated
for one (1) sex shall be used only by inmates of that sex;
(iii) Every shower room, sleeping quarters and restroom may be
redesignated if all inmates of the opposite sex vacate the area and the jail
provides notice to all employees.
(b) No inmate shall be placed in a shower room, sleeping quarters or
restroom that is designated for males or females unless the inmate is a member
of that sex or all members of the opposite sex have been moved to prohibit any
visual contact of the person of the opposite sex.

(c) Nothing in this section shall prohibit a jail employee from entering
shower rooms, sleeping quarters or restrooms under one (1) or more of the
following circumstances:
(i) If a jail employee is performing the employee's duties;
(ii) If there is a disaster or terroristic attack;
(iii) If it is necessary for the safety and security of the jail;
or
(iv) If it is necessary for a jail employee to establish order or
discipline.
(d) No jail shall be required to clearly post signage indicating the
designations for one (1) sex on entry points of shower rooms, sleeping quarters
or restrooms if jail employees and inmates are readily aware of the designation
for one (1) sex.
(e) An inmate placed or expressly allowed by a jail employee to enter a
shower room, sleeping quarter or restroom when other inmates of the opposite
sex are present shall have a cause of action against the jail provided the
inmate provides notice to a jail employee of an allegation to allow all video
and audio recordings in support of the claim to be retained. A civil action
initiated under this subsection shall be brought not later than one (1) year
after the violation occurred.
(f) An inmate not easily identifiable as male or female may be
administratively segregated for the safety and security of the inmate and other
inmates. An inmate who is administratively segregated under this subsection may
be temporarily allowed in a shower room, sleeping quarters or restroom
regardless of designation if the inmate is under the direct control of a jail
employee and there are no other shower rooms, sleeping quarters or restrooms
designated for single occupancy use. An inmate using a shower room, sleeping
quarters or restroom under this subsection shall be shielded from visual contact
of other inmates who are also using the shower room, sleeping quarters or
restroom.
(g) Nothing in this section shall prohibit an inmate or jail from using
any remedies afforded under the Prison Litigation Reduction Act to resolve any
violations of this section.". WILLIAMS
